@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy & data"; }
<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 760px">
    <h1 class="h3 mb-3">Privacy &amp; data</h1>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h6">What we store</h2>
        <p>Your account (email and a securely hashed password), your profile, diary entries, saved foods and meals, weight logs, goal history, and the text results of AI food scans.</p>
        <h2 class="h6">Food photos</h2>
        <p>Photos are checked and sent to the configured AI provider for analysis, then discarded. They are processed in memory and never saved on our server or in the database. The AI provider's own data policy applies to the image you send. For example, Google's free Gemini API tier may use submitted content to improve its products. Your profile details (age, weight and so on) are never sent to the AI provider.</p>
        <h2 class="h6">Your control</h2>
        <p class="mb-0">You can delete individual entries and scan records at any time, download your account data, or permanently delete your account and all of its data from <em>Profile &amp; Settings → Account</em>.</p>
    </div></div>
    <p class="disclaimer mt-3">Nutrition values, BMR/TDEE and AI estimates are approximations and are not medical advice. If you have a medical condition or need individual guidance, talk to a qualified healthcare professional.</p>
</div>
